; Regression test for GitHub issue #3314: the balanced virtual postings of
; a transaction, in [brackets], balance as a transaction of their own.
; Holding two commodities and no cost, they imply an exchange rate just
; as real postings do, and the rate that the real postings imply depends
; on the real postings alone.  Each group prices its own postings: the
; real ones change money at $1.10 a euro, the bracketed ones at $1.20.
; A cost written in one group leaves the other group to imply its own.

2020-01-01 Budget in euros
    [Budget:Travel]                   100.00 EUR
    [Budget:Checking]                $-110.00

2020-01-02 Change money
    [Budget:Travel]                   -50.00 EUR
    Assets:Wallet                      50.00 EUR
    Assets:Checking                   $-55.00
    [Budget:Checking]                  $60.00

2020-01-03 Buy shares
    Assets:Brokerage                    10 MSFT @ $200.00
    Assets:Checking                 $-2000.00
    [Budget:Shares]                     10 MSFT
    [Budget:Checking]               $-2000.00

test bal --flat
             10 MSFT  Assets:Brokerage
           $-2055.00  Assets:Checking
           50.00 EUR  Assets:Wallet
           $-2050.00  Budget:Checking
             10 MSFT  Budget:Shares
           50.00 EUR  Budget:Travel
--------------------
           $-4105.00
          100.00 EUR
             20 MSFT
end test

test bal --flat --basis
            $2000.00  Assets:Brokerage
           $-2055.00  Assets:Checking
              $55.00  Assets:Wallet
           $-2050.00  Budget:Checking
            $2000.00  Budget:Shares
              $50.00  Budget:Travel
--------------------
                   0
end test
